@crew pell
// Writer-commons, batch 1 (for the Voices sampler). Pell's card is the head writer's. Nothing about his mum's shop
// before tier friend; the music boxes are told from beat 1 (acquaintance), so the screw tin is safe there.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. New hand? Pell, Works. If it's broken, I've probably fixed it once.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}, {nick}. Is it morning? It feels like it shouldn't be morning.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Grab shelf's just been restocked. Act natural.
? tier>=colleague
- Calder looked at my weld and said "Fine." I'm having it framed.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {nick}! Sit down. I saved you a biscuit. Well, half. It was a long walk.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. Fixed a pump, ate twice, and nobody caught me napping.
? mood:low
- I'm fine. I'm fine. Just tired. Ask me again after a nap.

== near
? act:work
- Hold this. No, the other end. Perfect. You're a natural, {nick}.
? act:meal
- Is that pudding? Are you going to eat all of that pudding?   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Taught myself engines from an old manual. Half the pages were missing. Worked it out.
? tier>=colleague
- I talk in my sleep. About engines. Rina's taken notes. They're not flattering.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Every screw in this tin's from a ship I've fixed. One day they'll play a whole tune.

== week1
// The arrival evening, steps A9-A10: Pell joins your table in the mess (if he's there), before Calder stops by.
// Day 0 only: Sunday, before the week1.d2 flag. The head writer and onboarding may want an intro-step condition.
? week1:true weekday:sun time:evening !flag:week1.d2
- Oi oi. Mind if I sit? I'm Pell. Works. Bunk 2, next door to yours.
- You're the new hand! Brilliant. Has Torres talked your ear off yet? Give him time.   #funny
- A tip: the grab shelf. It's for emergencies. And me.   #funny
- Another tip: a panel on Deck 5 sticks. I'll show you which. Don't tell Calder.
- Eat the pudding first. Brennan's pudding goes fast and life's short.
- Welcome aboard, honestly. It's a good ship. Good people. You'll see.   #warm
? week1:true weekday:sun time:evening !flag:week1.d2 act:dinner
- Quick tip: the Chief's coming over. Sit up. Not that straight. Just normal straight.   #funny

// Writer-commons, batch 4: up to about 60. His mum's shop only from tier friend; the practical from beat:pell.5.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {nick}. Dinner was good. I had two. Don't tell Brennan. She knows.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Afternoon's the worst bit. Too late for a nap, too early for dinner.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- There you are! I was about to send a search party. Of one. Me. After lunch.   #funny
? tier>=colleague place:calm
- {hi}, {nick}. Pull up a seat. This one's warm. I've been warming it.
? tier>=close
- {nick}! Best person on the ship. Don't tell the others. Tell the others.   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Right, I'm off. Things to fix. Things to eat. Mostly eat.   #funny
- {bye}. Mind the Deck 5 panel. It bites.
? tier>=colleague time:night
- Night, {nick}. If you hear engine noises, that's me asleep. Ignore it.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Cheers for this. You're a good one, {nick}. I mean it.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Fed. Mostly awake. Can't ask for more.
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Bit flat. Mum's messages again. I'll be all right. Sit with me a minute?

== near
? act:leisure
- Screw tin's out. New music box. This one plays a sea shanty. Eventually.
? act:gym
- Gym. My idea. I regret it. I'll regret it less after lunch.   #funny
? deck:5
- Know which panel sticks? That one. Hip-height kick. Gently. Like a friend.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- I can sleep anywhere. Except my bunk, at night. Science can't explain it.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Mum runs a mending shop back home. Kettles, radios, coats. That's where I learnt.
? beat:pell.5
- Calder's practical. Every time I think of it, I need a biscuit. I've had a lot.   #funny

== invite
? trad:quiz tier>=acquaintance
- Quiz tonight. We need someone who knows the engines. And someone to eat my crisps. You in?
? trad:jam tier>=acquaintance
- Music jam tonight. I'm bringing a music box. Don't laugh. Laugh a bit.
? tier>=colleague time:evening
- Tea corner? I've got biscuits nobody's supposed to know about.

== accept
- Go on, then! I'll bring snacks. I always bring snacks.
- You bet. Wouldn't miss it. Unless I fall asleep. I won't. Probably.   #funny

== decline
- Ah, nuts. Can't. Calder's got me on a pump. Another time? Promise?
- Not tonight. I'm asleep. Well, I will be. Planning ahead.   #funny

== missed
- You weren't there! I ate your share. As a lesson. A delicious lesson.   #funny
- Missed you earlier. No harm done. Next time, eh?

== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I've told everyone. Twice. Is there cake? There's always cake.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, {nick}! I made you something. Three notes. The fourth's coming.   #warm

== hint
- Got a minute? A proper one. Not a Pell minute. Those are long.

== week1
? week1:true weekday:mon time:morning
- Morning, new hand! Tea break's ten-thirty. That's the important bit. The rest is work.
? week1:true weekday:wed tier<=acquaintance
- There you are. Settling in? Come and chat. Quiz is tomorrow. You're on my team now.
? week1:true weekday:thu time:evening
- Quiz night! Sit there. Know anything about engines? Good. Food? Even better.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance deck:4 time:night
- {hi}. Can't sleep. Classic Pell. I'll sleep at lunch. In a cupboard. Possibly.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance act:work
- {hi}, {nick}. Hand me that. No, that. Thanks. You're hired.

== near
? act:breakfast
- I'm awake. I'm awake! Is there toast? There's toast. Good. Now I'm awake.   #funny
? act:work
- Listen. Hear that? The bearing's going. Week, maybe. I'll put it on the board.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I nearly didn't come to the Wren. Best decision I nearly didn't make.
? tier>=colleague
- Found both secret biscuit tins aboard. Told nobody. I'm a vault. A hungry vault.   #funny

== feel
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Good day! Fixed a fan, found a biscuit, had a nap. In that order. Perfect.

== about
? aff:rina:friend
- Rina? Two years of insults. Best friend I've got. Don't tell her. She knows.   #warm
? bond:friends
- {friend}'s all right. Fed me when I forgot to eat. Twice. In one day.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 1: callbacks, visits and notes (the game adds his name to a note). Moment memories are
// moment.pell.<word> from beats 5-8. The handover's loose end: if you timed him (mem:moment.pell.timed), he says so
// once he's passed (beat 7).

== callback
? told:moment.pell.timed beat:pell.7
- You timed me every night. Then I passed. Those two things are related. I've checked.   #warm
? mem:moment.pell.timed !beat:pell.7
- Machine shop after shift? You bring the watch. I'll bring the nerves. And biscuits.
? told:moment.pell.cheered
- "A pump's nothing." I've been saying it to myself. Out loud. Halloran's worried.   #funny
? told:moment.pell.listened
- Cheers for sitting with me. For the messages. I slept after. At night! A first.   #warm
? told:moment.pell.mechanic
- "Raised a mechanic in a scrapyard." I told Mum you said that. She's chuffed to bits.   #warm
? told:moment.pell.help
- That lad two doors down? I've sent him three lessons. He's hopeless. He's getting better.   #funny
? told:moment.pell.knew
- You knew I'd pass. You were right. Don't let it go to your head. Let it go a bit.   #funny
? told:moment.pell.glad
- Still here. Still glad. Don't go soppy on me. Have a biscuit.   #warm
? told:moment.pell.why
- Pudding and a pump. That's what kept me. I told Brennan. She gave me more pudding.   #funny
? told:moment.pell.shared
- Still unpacked? Good. I'll know if you pack. I know everything in the junior wing.   #funny
? told:show.pell-show
- You came to the music boxes. I saw you. The waltz went better because of it.   #warm
? told:came.quiz
- You came to quiz! We came fourth. Out of five. That's nearly a medal.   #funny
? told:came.jam
- Cheers for coming to the jam. The music box went down a storm. Well. Nobody left.   #funny
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it! I'd have fetched it after a nap. A long nap. You're a legend.   #funny
? told:fav.lamp
- My lamp's fixed. I can see my screws now. Turns out half of them are bolts.   #funny
? told:fav.job
- You did my job! Calder thinks it was me. I'll tell her. Tomorrow. Cheers, {nick}.   #funny
? told:gift.sweet
- Those sweets lasted a whole day. A record. Well, an afternoon. Cheers.   #funny
? told:gift.tea
- Your tea's in my locker. I make it when I can't sleep. So, every night.   #funny
? told:gift.made
- The thing you made me's on the shelf, next to the screw tin. Pride of place.   #warm
? told:gift.music
- Played your music all through my shift. Calder hummed. I swear she hummed.   #funny
? told:fixed.pump
- You sorted the pumps? Clean work. That's what Calder says. Now I'm saying it.
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday! And you didn't even make me share the cake. Legend.   #funny
? told:grubby
- You were grubbier than me yesterday. Never thought I'd see the day. Respect.   #funny
? told:heard.moment.rina
- Rina likes you. She won't say. She's stopped counting your losses out loud. Huge.   #funny
? told:heard.moment.tomas
- Tomas reckons you're the best thing on the Wren. After the stars. Close second.   #warm

== visit
- Oi oi. Brought snacks. Don't ask from where. Shove up.   #funny
- Couldn't sleep. Course I couldn't, it's night. Fancy a natter?   #funny
- New music box. Three notes. Listen. No, that was two. Hang on.
- Right, so. I was passing. I wasn't. I came on purpose. Biscuit?   #warm
- Tomas let me in. He said you'd be glad. Are you glad? Say yes.   #funny

== note
- Came by. You were out. I ate one of your biscuits and left you the other. Fair's fair.   #funny
- Found a good spanner. It's on your pillow. Don't tell Calder where I found it.   #funny
- Grab shelf's just been restocked. Act natural. You didn't hear it from me.
- Knocked, nobody home. Tea corner tomorrow? I'll bring the nice biscuits.
- Fell asleep on your bunk waiting for you. Sorry about the dent.   #funny
